Kermit the Frog wrote:

> You don't need to wear the Eye to have the bonus power regeneration.
> It only has to be in your inventory.  

True.

> The only thing you get by wearing 
> the eye is telepathy (which you presumably already have from eating the
> floating eye).

You get ESP by wearing the Amulet; telepathy (which you get from eating a
floating eye) is a subset of that. ESP lets you see all monsters with a
brain within a certain range whether you're blind or not, and all
monsters with a brain on the level when you're blind. Telepathy gives
only the blind effect. (Enlightenment will tell you "You are telepathic"
in both cases, not completely helpful)

> Better bet yet is probably Amulet of Life Saving.

If you want that; some people avoid wearing amulets of life saving as an
unofficial conduct.

> It's very important.  You definitely want it against Rodney.  However,
> if
> Rodney steals your Eye, he becomes immune to the finger.  Just drop him
> dead before he steals anything from ye.

And after you have the Amulet, it takes *lots* of Pw and you're probably
better off casting magic missile if you're high enough level to make it
really kick ass.

>> What is cancellation good for?  I haven't used it much.  Does it work
>> on mind flayers?
> 
> Yes, it does.

And it uncurses whole stacks of cursed things, and bags of holding
(without affecting the contents). You can cast it at yourself when all
your stuff gets cursed as long as you drop everything you don't want
cancelled; your whole inventory will become uncursed +0. Contrary to
common belief, it will *not* affect *your* intrinsics. 

>> Also I seem to remember that /oCold and /oFire are good for end game.
>> Should I be saving these?

Keep one wand of cold with at least one charge for the eventuality that
you get stuck in lava on the Plane of Fire. If that happens, break it and
you'll be stuck in rock that you can dig yourself out of (so don't throw
away your pick-axe on leaving Earth).

